      "_key": "!journal.pages!OSMVQHNXfk9zRyLM.wIHnBJ2rJOy55OvS",
      "name": "Read Aloud",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<section class=\"sbn-leer\"><p>At the top of the hill stands a Victorian house with a green copper dome that was once a private observatory. The dome still opens. What pokes out through the slit isn&#39;t a telescope but an antenna. Inside, carved wood paneling shares the walls with server racks and screens showing network traffic graphs.</p>\n</section>\n"
      },
